+/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
+	Local corrections for a conforming compiler.
+
+	This file shipped with the Unreal 224 SDK and predates standard C++. The changes below are the
+	only edits to it, and each one is how Unreal 226 already spells the same code:
+
+	* The ten explicit TTypeInfo specialisations derived from TTypeInfoBase<T>, naming a template
+	  parameter that is not in scope in a specialisation. Each now names its own type, so
+	  TTypeInfo<INT> derives from TTypeInfoBase<INT> and inherits the ConstInitType that TMap and
+	  TArray ask it for.
+
+	* TMap::TPair, TMap::Add/AddUnique/Set/Remove/RemovePair and TMap::TFinder took
+	  TTypeInfo<TK>::ConstInitType without 'typename'. It is a dependent type and needs the keyword.
+
+	* FString::InStrRight read its inner loop counter after the loop, which is out of scope. The
+	  declaration is hoisted, leaving the loop and the read as they were.
+
+	The renderers do not call any of this themselves; it has to compile because Core.h reaches it.
+
+	See patch_unreal_224_sdk.ps1 at the repository root for why these are here rather than in the
+	renderers' own headers.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
 
